How to Run the Project

Step 1: Open Project Folder

Open terminal and navigate to the project directory:

cd StayWiseProject
Step 2: Create Virtual Environment
python -m venv venv
Step 3: Activate Virtual Environment


Windows:

venv\Scripts\activate
Step 4: Install Required Packages
pip install flask pandas joblib scikit-learn
Step 5: Run the Application
python app.py
Step 6: Open in Browser


Go to:

http://127.0.0.1:5000
Login Credentials
Email: admin@staywise.com  
Password: 123456
Application Flow

User logs into the system

Enters customer details

System sends data to Flask backend

Machine learning model predicts churn probability

Result is displayed with visualization

Prediction is stored in database

Dashboard shows analytics

Database

SQLite database (predictions.db) is automatically created

Stores last predictions with timestamp

Used for dashboard analytics

Notes

Ensure model.pkl is present in the root directory

Do not rename template or static folders

Run the app from the same directory where app.py exists

Future Improvements

Secure authentication system

Model explainability (feature importance)

Advanced analytics dashboard

Dataset upload functionality

Deployment on cloud platform


Conclusion

StayWise demonstrates how machine learning can be integrated with web technologies to solve real-world business problems such as customer churn prediction.